  "reconstruction_algorithm": {
    "PARK_January_June": "Start with saved $2,000 cash and zero positions. Restrict full historical modeled fills to January 1 < fill timestamp <= July 1 boundary. For each original canonical asset, purchases minus sales must equal exact June surviving lot quantity; all-in acquisition costs minus released fee-inclusive basis must equal the surviving lot basis. Reconcile cash, fees and realized P&L to the frozen checkpoint under exported source-rounding tolerances.",
    "PARK_July": "Use exact June boundary active lots and 29 saved modeled fills with June boundary < fill timestamp <= July 31 boundary. Map each terminal lot:<buy order ID> to its unique genuine historical ENTRY/RECOVERY fill. Check original/current quantity and fee-inclusive basis, then reconcile each asset and total cash/basis/fees against the unchanged saved PARK control. Do not use a redeployment arm inventory as PARK.",
    "PARK_July_marks": "Use the prior SHA-verified independent actual-tape terminal mark receipt at the identical frozen boundary. Require every shared asset price/timestamp/age to agree across arms, every mark timestamp <= cutoff, and age = cutoff minus timestamp. Multiply the exact PARK units by that asset market mark and require the aggregate to match saved PARK inventory within $1e-18. These are historical last closes, not current executable prices.",
    "concentration": "Compute HHI from owned inventory market-value weights and effective holdings as 1/HHI. Compute acquisition-basis concentration separately. Report cash separately, preserve every owned residual and do not sum heterogeneous asset units."
  },
  "rounding_tolerances": {
